      "type": "text",
      "text": "I've marked the run as anomalous and asked for a person to check it (recorded only; the run continues regardless).\n\n- **What changed:** during growth, tube pressure climbed steadily from about 3.04 to 3.48 Torr between t=2640 s and t=3240 s. Argon flow stayed at about 100 sccm throughout, so the flow setting isn't the cause.\n- **Still normal:** temperature is holding at 750 °C with normal heater power. Pressure was steady at about 3.0 Torr through the ramp.\n- **Likely causes:** either air leaking in through a seal or a partly blocked exhaust. I can't tell which, because this furnace has no exhaust O2 sensor, so the growth atmosphere can't be checked with the installed sensors.\n- **What would settle it:** isolate the gas flow and see whether pressure keeps rising (a leak-up test), or inspect the pump and exhaust line.\n- **Scientific result:** the sample hasn't been characterized yet. If this continues, any result will likely be inconclusive rather than evidence about the recipe."
     }
